.TH DANBY-STABILITY 1
.SH NAME
danby-stability \- compare linear and nonlinear stability
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/stability
.SH DESCRIPTION
The laboratory overlays a nonlinear trajectory (green) and the trajectory
predicted by linearization (ochre).  The parameter
.I a
is the real part of the linear eigenvalues.
.PP
For negative values the origin is a stable focus.  For positive values it is
unstable, while the nonlinear saturation creates a stable limit cycle of
radius square-root(a).  At zero the linear test is inconclusive but the cubic
terms establish nonlinear asymptotic stability.  This makes visible both the
power and the limitation of linear stability analysis.
.SH SEE ALSO
danby-modeling(1), numerics(2), plot(2)
